\title{Categorical Tropicalization of Interleaving Distance \\ and Vietoris--Rips Stability}
\author{Aristotle (Harmonic)}
\date{2026-06-15}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We develop, in a deliberately minimal order-theoretic setting, the algebraic and
geometric core of persistence stability and exhibit its tropical (min-plus)
nature. A \emph{persistence module} is modeled as a monotone map
$M : \R \to \alpha$ into a preorder $\alpha$; an \emph{$\varepsilon$-interleaving}
of two modules is a pair of $\varepsilon$-shifted dominations. We prove that
interleavings form a reflexive, symmetric system that is monotone in the shift
and, crucially, \emph{composable with additive shifts}: an
$\varepsilon$-interleaving followed by a $\delta$-interleaving is an
$(\varepsilon+\delta)$-interleaving. From this composition law we build the
\emph{interleaving distance} $\idist$ valued in $\Rinf = [0,\infty]$ and prove it
is an extended pseudometric. The triangle inequality is shown to be
\emph{literally} a statement of tropical algebra: under the embedding
$\trop : \Rinf \to \mathrm{Tropical}\,\Rinf$ (multiplication is ordinary
addition, addition is infimum), it is exactly submultiplicativity,
$\trop\,d(M,L) \leq \trop\,d(M,N) \cdot \trop\,d(N,L)$. Specializing to
\emph{Vietoris--Rips modules} of a dissimilarity $d : X \to X \to \R$, modeled by
edge sets $\{(x,y) : d\,x\,y \leq t\}$ in the lattice $\mathrm{Set}(X\times X)$,
we prove \emph{stability}: sup-close dissimilarities yield interleaved modules,
hence $\idist(\RipsMod d, \RipsMod d') \leq \ofReal\,\lVert d - d'\rVert_\infty$.
All results are fully formally verified. We close with five falsifiable
conjectures.
\end{abstract}

